.TH SPRITEPUTEXT 1
.SH NAME
spriteputext \- a sprite borrowed from another file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spriteputext
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I SpritePutExt
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/SpritePutExt.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The US map three times, drawn from a sprite this program does not
contain.  The original names another source file and the number of a
sprite inside it, so editing that file changes this picture; the warning
in the original is that the number breaks if the sprites in the target
file are reordered.  Here the borrowed asset belongs to
.IR spriteput (1).
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/spriteputext.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR spriteedit (1),
.IR wm (1)
